  "labelNotes": "No Recommended Operating Conditions table; the supply range is printed only in the DC Characteristics header lines (Industrial: VCC +1.7 to +5.5 V at TA -40 to 85 C; Automotive: VCC +2.5 to +5.5 V at TA -40 to 125 C). Labelled as MIN/MAX with the TA printed in the same cell as conditions - judgement call, since these are header lines rather than a parameter row. D9 conditions 'VCC = 5.5V, SCL = 400 kHz' mapped to VCC = 5.5 V, F = 400 kHz (SCL clock frequency treated as F - judgement call). D10 (ICC read) prints '-' in its conditions cell, so no conditions. D11 standby: 0.01 TYP / 1 MAX uA (Industrial) and 5 MAX uA (Automotive); grade names and SDA=SCL=VCC/WP=VSS are not allowed condition keys. ILI printed as '+/-1' uA in the MAX column; labelled as 1 uA MAX. ILO (output leakage) excluded. Abs max VCC 6.5 V; 'All inputs and outputs ... -0.3V to VCC +1.0V' is an expression, skipped. Standby unit printed with a Greek capital Alpha ('\u03bc\u0391'), normalised to uA."
